[00:09.01]A: I used to rule the world
[00:12.70]B: Seas would rise when I gave the word
[00:15.18]A: Now in the morning, I sleep alone
[00:19.50]B: Sweep the streets I used to own
[00:36.49]A: I used to roll the dice
[00:40.55]B: Feel the fear in my enemy's eyes
[00:43.81]A: Listened as the crowd would sing
[00:47.62]AB: "Now the old king is dead, long live the king"
[00:50.46]A: One minute I held the key
[00:54.43]B: Next, the walls were closed on me
[00:57.10]A: And I discovered that my castles stand
[01:01.36]B: Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand
[01:05.18]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[01:09.06]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[01:12.52]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[01:15.64]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[01:19.44]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[01:22.84]B: Once you'd gone, there was never
[01:25.47]A: Never an honest word
[01:29.18]AB: And that was when I ruled the world
[01:45.83]A: It was a wicked and wild wind
[01:50.00]B: Blew down the doors to let me in
[01:52.69]A: Shattered windows and the sound of drums
[01:57.05]B: People couldn't believe what I'd become
[02:00.24]A: Revolutionaries wait
[02:04.08]B: For my head on a silver plate
[02:06.53]A: Just a puppet on a lonely string
[02:11.10]B: Oh, who would ever want to be king?
[02:14.87]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[02:18.47]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[02:21.88]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[02:25.34]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[02:28.82]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[02:32.40]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[02:35.59]A: Never an honest word
[02:38.66]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
[03:11.00]AB: Hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[03:14.05]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[03:17.63]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[03:20.91]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[03:24.53]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[03:27.99]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
